# Keyboard-first POS

Every billing and report action must be usable without a mouse. The app must also feel like a Windows native WinForms POS (see `windows-native.mdc`), not a website.

- Put a visible Tab order on Table No, Card No, Waiter, ItemName, and function keys.
- Wire the labeled shortcuts: F1 Complim., F3 Create Item (Item Master: add, edit, delete), F4 Item transfer, F5 Save, F7 KOT report, F8 Bill report, F9 table transfer, F10 Prepare Bill, F11 Settlement, F12 S. Report. Escape blanks Table/Card No and the item list and does not save. Escape closes Item Master.
- Enter confirms the focused field (select/create table, load card, add item, settle).
- Alt+1 THE BOSS CLUB, Alt+2 RESTAURANT, Alt+3 NC, Alt+4 BAR. Ctrl+Right and Ctrl+Left move to the next and previous department in that order, wrapping around. Ctrl+Shift+Right and Ctrl+Shift+Left do the same.
- Default focus is Card No on THE BOSS CLUB (Enter loads the card and moves to Table No; Enter on Table No opens the table and moves to ItemName). Default focus is Table No on BAR, NC, and RESTAURANT; Enter then moves to ItemName.
- Enter on ItemName with no item selected stays on ItemName. Do not move to Remark. Enter accepts a highlighted catalog item and moves to Qty. Enter on Qty saves that line (qty default 1, or -1 to reduce a running order) and opens a new ItemName row. Enter on Remark focuses Print KOT (F16). Enter on Print KOT saves, prints the KOT, then blanks the table like Escape.
- Item lookup stays blank until a letter is typed. Do not prefill the full catalog. After Print KOT the table selection, card, and punch grid clear, the same as Escape, and the right pane returns to Table Estimate.
- When no table is open, the right pane is Table Estimate. After Table No Enter on a running table, the right pane is Table No. Items List (Code, ItemName, Qty) with Estimate at the bottom. Punch -1 qty of an item and Print KOT to modify/reduce a running order.
- F10 Prepare Bill first lists running tables (Up/Down, Enter). After a table is chosen, the Restaurant Bill dialog opens with focus on Discount (%). Enter on Discount moves to Print Bill (F10). Print Bill generates the invoice and the table shows as Settlement (green) on the estimate list. Save (F5), or the Save button, asks Do you want to save? Yes saves the bill and opens Restaurant Settlement. It does not ask to print.
- F11 Settlement first lists tables that already have a printed bill (Up/Down, Enter), same picker as F10. Enter opens Restaurant Settlement, identical to clicking Settlement on the estimate list. Settled Amount is the current payment (green). Balance Amount is what remains. The dialog opens with focus on Settled Amount. Enter moves to Payment Mode, which defaults to CASH. Up/Down on Payment Mode changes CASH, BANK TRANSFER, and PREPAID CARD. Enter on CASH moves to the Save button. BANK TRANSFER shows Bank Name on the next row under Payment Mode (Bank payment, BOOK MY SHOW, COUPON, DINEOUT, DISTRICT, EAZYDINNER, HDFC, PAYTM, ZOMATO, PARTYPAL, INDUS, MOBIKWIK); Enter on Payment Mode moves there, Up/Down changes the bank, and Enter moves to Save. PREPAID CARD shows Card No under Payment Mode as a combobox of cards recharged today. Type a card number or press Up/Down to pick one; the edit shows only what was typed. Enter on Payment Mode moves there. Enter on Card No settles from that card immediately: if the balance is positive, deduct the smaller of the card balance and the settled amount (a ₹1000 card against a ₹3000 settlement takes ₹1000 and leaves the rest; a ₹4000 card against a ₹1000 settlement takes ₹1000). If the balance is not positive, show Insufficient amount with the card’s current balance and return focus to Settled Amount. Save (F2) uses the same card amount. Enter on Save posts that amount. Save (F2) posts from any field. If the bill is not fully settled, the same dialog stays open, Payment Mode returns to CASH, and focus returns to Settled Amount (the remaining due). Stay on the dialog until the balance is 0; split a bill across modes on the same screen.
- F12 Settlement Report: Enter or double-click a row opens the same Restaurant Settlement dialog. Focus starts on Settled Amount. Enter moves to Payment Mode. Up/Down changes CASH, BANK TRANSFER, and PREPAID CARD. Enter on CASH moves to Update (F2). BANK TRANSFER shows Bank Name under Payment Mode; Up/Down changes the bank and Enter moves to Update. PREPAID CARD shows Card No under Payment Mode; Enter checks the card and shows Insufficient amount with the card balance when it is short. Buttons stay Print, Update (F2), Delete (F4), and Exit. Escape closes the dialog and leaves the report open.
- On a selected line, a letter or number blanks the name and opens suggestions. Enter accepts the item and moves to Qty. Qty accepts more than one digit. Up/Down on the name, when the list is closed, selects the previous or next punched line and shows that line’s qty. Enter on Qty saves that qty for the same item. Left/Right on a new line’s Qty steps the catalog item; Qty stays.
- Backspace after a chosen item does not wipe the name: the item stays and turns black. Further Backspace deletes one character at a time. Backspace on Qty (when 1 is selected) returns to ItemName with the item still there.
- Item lookup is a Windows combobox: type a letter (e.g. K) to list matching items. The edit field shows only what was typed; the first match is selected once in the list (blue). Do not also fill that name into the edit field. Enter takes it. Up/Down move the selection.
- Table No is typed and confirmed with Enter on THE BOSS CLUB, BAR, NC, and RESTAURANT. Do not use a dropdown on the main billing Table No. THE BOSS CLUB asks Card No first, then Table No directly under that Card No. The balance-check Card No stays on the right of the department bar on every tab, including THE BOSS CLUB. Every Card No in the app accepts digits only, four digits maximum. A letter or a fifth digit is ignored. If the number is not four digits, do not alert; keep focus on that Card No. If a card is entered and its balance is below the item amount, show Insufficient amount with the card’s current balance.
- Do not add a flow that only works by clicking.

```tsx
// BAD
<button onClick={prepareBill}>Prepare Bill</button>

// GOOD
<button onClick={prepareBill}>Prepare Bill (F10)</button>
// and F10 in the window keydown handler calls prepareBill()
```
